<section_header_level_1><loc_156><loc_55><loc_440><loc_63>A CHARACTERIZATION OF WEIGHTED ARITHMETIC MEANS*</section_header_level_1>
<text><loc_245><loc_68><loc_351><loc_75>J. ACZÉL? AND C. WAGNER?</text>
<text><loc_140><loc_79><loc_456><loc_92>Abstract. We prove, among other things, that the set of weighted arithmetic means is identical with the set of functions f: R" -> R satisfying</text>
<text><loc_154><loc_94><loc_274><loc_101>(i) min {x} = f(x1, x2, · · · , x) = max {x}</text>
<text><loc_140><loc_103><loc_152><loc_109>(ii)</text>
<text><loc_157><loc_103><loc_168><loc_109>for</text>
